From 44b45c216f778cbcb442a84989d8b71bbbfbe463 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:20:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Let the default terminal setting choose the terminal

The image put a Foot-only xdg-terminal-exec in /usr/local/bin, ahead of the
packaged one on PATH. Super+Return, the Omarchy menu and the default terminal
check mark all went through it, so choosing another terminal never applied
(#385). The packaged xdg-terminal-exec already follows Omarchy's list, which
starts with Foot, and Omarchy's foot.desktop carries the app id, title and
directory arguments the shim used to translate.

Stop shipping the shim. Catch-up removes it from existing disks when it is
still the unchanged copy, and compatibility revision 66 delivers that.
